1
00:01:35,450 --> 00:01:36,660
Senpai.

2
00:01:40,630 --> 00:01:43,250
Are you awake?

3
00:01:44,420 --> 00:01:46,260
Good morning, Sakura.

4
00:01:50,010 --> 00:01:53,010
Yes, good morning, Senpai.

5
00:01:57,310 --> 00:01:59,099
Sorry, Sakura.

6
00:01:59,100 --> 00:02:02,479
I should be helping
with breakfast.

7
00:02:02,480 --> 00:02:04,819
Don't worry about that.

8
00:02:04,820 --> 00:02:07,029
You were up late
again, weren't you?

9
00:02:07,030 --> 00:02:09,360
Don't be silly.
That's no excuse.

10
00:02:09,860 --> 00:02:13,700
Let me take care of it, Senpai.

11
00:02:14,410 --> 00:02:19,620
If you leave the storehouse in this
state, Fujimura-sensei will scold you.

12
00:02:21,420 --> 00:02:23,289
Good point.

13
00:02:23,290 --> 00:02:25,379
Guess I'll take you
up on that offer, then.

14
00:02:25,380 --> 00:02:26,419
Great.

15
00:02:26,420 --> 00:02:28,590
I'll be waiting for you, Senpai.

16
00:02:30,720 --> 00:02:34,890
Falling asleep before
finishing shows that I lack focus.

17
00:02:56,120 --> 00:03:01,160
In the face of absolute despair

18
00:03:01,460 --> 00:03:05,160
That nearly burned
our hearts away

19
00:03:06,660 --> 00:03:11,710
You still found the
courage to smile

20
00:03:11,960 --> 00:03:16,510
Like you accepted it all

21
00:03:17,310 --> 00:03:19,770
I lost my voice

22
00:03:19,970 --> 00:03:22,390
And the things I wanted to say

23
00:03:22,670 --> 00:03:27,640
But every time I
fell to my knees

24
00:03:27,990 --> 00:03:31,940
I stood up and kept walking

25
00:03:32,210 --> 00:03:37,610
We were looking for
the ideal white future

26
00:03:37,820 --> 00:03:42,840
Our one and only hope

27
00:03:43,170 --> 00:03:45,330
Now I may be left with nothing

28
00:03:45,500 --> 00:03:50,750
But these raging
emotions that have

29
00:03:50,810 --> 00:03:53,850
Nowhere to go

30
00:03:54,100 --> 00:03:59,100
Still, I'll look for a new dawn

31
00:03:59,480 --> 00:04:02,510
With more than one right answer

32
00:04:02,750 --> 00:04:06,340
I won't stop

33
00:04:06,640 --> 00:04:08,370
Until I find it

34
00:04:15,160 --> 00:04:19,490
A Winter's Day, A Fateful Night

35
00:04:29,840 --> 00:04:31,759
In other news,

36
00:04:31,760 --> 00:04:33,630
the government
announced this morning

37
00:04:32,300 --> 00:04:33,300
Perfect.

38
00:04:33,630 --> 00:04:38,140
That it has approved the merger
between KK Aviation and TT Airways.

39
00:04:39,930 --> 00:04:45,309
There were concerns that the
proposed deal would violate antitrust laws,

40
00:04:45,310 --> 00:04:47,104
but it was given the
green light after the two

41
00:04:47,116 --> 00:04:49,000
companies agreed to
scale down their operations.

42
00:04:49,001 --> 00:04:50,939
I feel terrible making
you do all this, Sakura.

43
00:04:50,940 --> 00:04:53,110
It's no trouble at all.

44
00:04:53,360 --> 00:04:55,900
I do it because I want to.

45
00:04:57,200 --> 00:04:59,119
Morning, Fuji-nee.

46
00:04:59,120 --> 00:05:01,280
Morning!

47
00:05:03,700 --> 00:05:04,909
Let's eat!

48
00:05:04,910 --> 00:05:06,120
Let's eat.

49
00:05:19,300 --> 00:05:20,390
Senpai?

50
00:05:20,720 --> 00:05:23,929
Th-This isn't soy sauce!

51
00:05:23,930 --> 00:05:27,560
Other sauces don't belong on rice with
grated yams! Especially not oyster sauce!

52
00:05:29,150 --> 00:05:34,150
I switched the labels on the
bottles earlier! Gotcha good, huh?

53
00:05:34,530 --> 00:05:35,530
Yay!

54
00:05:35,860 --> 00:05:38,569
Who pulls a stunt like that
first thing in the morning?

55
00:05:38,570 --> 00:05:40,810
You're turning twenty-five
this year, for heaven's sake.

56
00:05:41,320 --> 00:05:43,989
Guess you'll always be
the same old Fuji-nee.

57
00:05:43,990 --> 00:05:45,579
You had it coming!

58
00:05:45,580 --> 00:05:47,710
This is payback for yesterday!

59
00:05:48,460 --> 00:05:49,709
Senpai, have some tea.

60
00:05:49,710 --> 00:05:52,089
I thought you
seemed awfully quiet.

61
00:05:52,090 --> 00:05:55,089
You've been planning
this ever since then?

62
00:05:55,090 --> 00:05:56,839
Damn straight.

63
00:05:56,840 --> 00:06:00,720
I spent a whole lot of time that I
should have spent grading tests.

64
00:06:01,300 --> 00:06:04,180
So I gotta run, or I'll never
get them done in time!

65
00:06:05,720 --> 00:06:07,230
Thanks for breakfast!

66
00:06:08,730 --> 00:06:10,730
See you at school!

67
00:06:11,150 --> 00:06:15,189
Don't go back to sleep
and wind up late, okay?

68
00:06:15,190 --> 00:06:17,490
Well, I'm outta here!

69
00:06:19,360 --> 00:06:22,570
Your cooking was as
delicious as ever, Sakura-chan!

70
00:06:24,660 --> 00:06:28,960
It was nothing, Fujimura-sensei.

71
00:06:32,250 --> 00:06:33,250
Soy

72
00:06:33,251 --> 00:06:34,250
Oyster

73
00:06:32,580 --> 00:06:34,250
Damn that Fuji-nee.

74
00:06:34,500 --> 00:06:39,009
Does being the landlord's daughter
give her the right to eat here every day?

75
00:06:39,010 --> 00:06:41,380
She's no better
than a freeloader.

76
00:06:45,350 --> 00:06:48,809
Did you do something
to upset her yesterday?

77
00:06:48,810 --> 00:06:51,019
I accidentally called her
by that one nickname.

78
00:06:51,020 --> 00:06:53,150
Then you deserved it, Senpai.

79
00:06:53,560 --> 00:06:54,859
You should be more careful.

80
00:06:54,860 --> 00:06:59,280
You know she hates it
when you call her that.

81
00:07:03,200 --> 00:07:05,700
- Tokyo - Gas Leak in
Shinto Business District

82
00:07:04,070 --> 00:07:05,700
In our next story,

83
00:07:06,200 --> 00:07:11,079
workers in a Shinto business
district office building were hospitalized

84
00:07:11,080 --> 00:07:14,209
after passing
out late last night.

85
00:07:14,210 --> 00:07:15,790
According to the
police statement,

86
00:07:15,791 --> 00:07:17,715
Tokyo

87
00:07:17,716 --> 00:07:21,220
Gas Leak in Shinto
Business District

88
00:07:15,790 --> 00:07:18,444
the victims were all found
with apparent hypoxia, which

89
00:07:18,456 --> 00:07:21,219
has led them to suspect a
possible gas leak as the cause.

90
00:07:21,220 --> 00:07:23,640
However, given that a similar
incident occurred last month,

91
00:07:21,840 --> 00:07:24,220
Hear that? Another
gas leak in Shinto.

92
00:07:24,221 --> 00:07:28,060
They are also investigating
a possible connection.

93
00:07:24,840 --> 00:07:26,719
That's messed up.

94
00:07:26,720 --> 00:07:28,429
We need to be careful too.

95
00:07:28,430 --> 00:07:30,230
Don't worry.

96
00:07:30,890 --> 00:07:36,110
I always double-check the
gas valve, so we'll be fine.

97
00:07:37,860 --> 00:07:41,360
No, not about that.

98
00:07:50,120 --> 00:07:52,120
Well, work hard
at club practice.

99
00:07:53,710 --> 00:07:55,669
About that, Senpai...

100
00:07:55,670 --> 00:07:59,299
Maybe you could
stop by the dojo?

101
00:07:59,300 --> 00:08:01,880
I have to go to the student
council office this morning.

102
00:08:03,720 --> 00:08:06,009
O-Oh, of course.

103
00:08:06,010 --> 00:08:09,260
I'm sorry. Forget I asked.

104
00:08:10,770 --> 00:08:12,769
Well, I should get going.

105
00:08:12,770 --> 00:08:15,350
Look forward to
dinner tonight, okay?

106
00:08:20,940 --> 00:08:24,109
The school's budgetary allocations
are completely unbalanced.

107
00:08:24,110 --> 00:08:28,449
Yeah, athletic clubs get the lion's share
of the budget, and the rest get the crumbs.

108
00:08:28,450 --> 00:08:29,450
Indeed.

109
00:08:29,780 --> 00:08:33,039
As a result, the facilities available
to non-athletic clubs are in disrepair.

110
00:08:33,040 --> 00:08:35,750
They've given zero thought
to resolving our heater issues.

111
00:08:36,460 --> 00:08:38,839
You mean this isn't
the only broken one?

112
00:08:38,840 --> 00:08:39,840
Indeed.

113
00:08:41,130 --> 00:08:43,510
As I thought, it's
just showing its age.

114
00:08:44,010 --> 00:08:45,629
Can you fix it, Emiya?

115
00:08:45,630 --> 00:08:46,510
I can.

116
00:08:46,511 --> 00:08:48,010
Really?

117
00:08:48,300 --> 00:08:51,600
It won't take long, so
could you wait outside?

118
00:08:52,930 --> 00:08:55,140
Of course. I'll get
out of your way.

119
00:08:58,650 --> 00:09:00,150
Okay, then.

120
00:09:06,820 --> 00:09:11,409
There are two spots where the
heating element is about to break.

121
00:09:11,410 --> 00:09:13,750
The heat transfer pipes
should be good for a while.

122
00:09:16,500 --> 00:09:19,920
I can patch the power cord
with electrical tape for now.

123
00:09:31,550 --> 00:09:32,890
Tohsaka...

124
00:09:34,350 --> 00:09:35,639
Tohsaka?

125
00:09:35,640 --> 00:09:37,599
Well, if it isn't the
student council president.

126
00:09:37,600 --> 00:09:40,649
Already up and
patrolling the school?

127
00:09:40,650 --> 00:09:43,319
Or are you doing
maintenance on the club rooms?

128
00:09:43,320 --> 00:09:46,150
Either way, I see you're
as diligent as always.

129
00:09:47,110 --> 00:09:49,660
And what are you
up to this morning?

130
00:09:50,410 --> 00:09:54,199
Why are you here so early
when you aren't in any clubs?

131
00:09:54,200 --> 00:09:56,160
I just felt like it.

132
00:09:58,160 --> 00:10:00,329
It's fixed, Issei.

133
00:10:00,330 --> 00:10:01,839
Oh, sorry.

134
00:10:01,840 --> 00:10:05,209
I asked you for help, but you
ended up doing all the work.

135
00:10:05,210 --> 00:10:06,419
My bad, Emiya.

136
00:10:06,420 --> 00:10:08,379
Where's the next one?

137
00:10:08,380 --> 00:10:09,759
We don't have all day.

138
00:10:09,760 --> 00:10:12,259
It's in the A/V room.

139
00:10:12,260 --> 00:10:14,883
They said it had been
acting up for a while, and now

140
00:10:14,895 --> 00:10:17,479
it looks like it's reached
the end of its lifespan.

141
00:10:17,480 --> 00:10:19,890
If it's dead, I can't fix that.

142
00:10:20,230 --> 00:10:21,809
You're better off
buying a new one.

143
00:10:21,810 --> 00:10:25,229
While that's true, I'd appreciate it if
you could take a look at it anyway.

144
00:10:25,230 --> 00:10:29,399
It looked dead to me, but you might
be able to tell if it's just pretending.

145
00:10:29,400 --> 00:10:31,570
Okay. I'll give it a shot.

146
00:10:38,120 --> 00:10:41,000
You're an early riser, Tohsaka.

147
00:10:50,590 --> 00:10:52,889
The art club's heater will
have to wait until lunchtime.

148
00:10:52,890 --> 00:10:54,049
Yeah.

149
00:10:54,050 --> 00:10:56,760
You're quite the busy
bee this morning, Emiya.

150
00:10:57,350 --> 00:11:00,229
I was wondering what you'd
been up to after quitting the club.

151
00:11:00,230 --> 00:11:02,520
You're the student council
president's errand boy, eh?

152
00:11:04,860 --> 00:11:07,609
If you need anything on your
end, just let me know, Shinji.

153
00:11:07,610 --> 00:11:09,989
If it's something I
can help with, I will.

154
00:11:09,990 --> 00:11:13,530
Maintaining bows was
never your strong suit, after all.

155
00:11:15,620 --> 00:11:17,289
Mind your own business.

156
00:11:17,290 --> 00:11:22,920
You're not part of the club anymore, so
don't show your face near the dojo again!

157
00:11:23,370 --> 00:11:26,230
Is he serious? Did he
forget that he was the

158
00:11:26,242 --> 00:11:28,919
one who drove you
out in the first place?

159
00:11:28,920 --> 00:11:31,969
It's okay. That's
just how he is.

160
00:11:31,970 --> 00:11:33,680
You get used to it eventually.

161
00:11:34,510 --> 00:11:35,969
Do you, now?

162
00:11:35,970 --> 00:11:37,600
You do.

163
00:11:38,350 --> 00:11:41,680
Uh-oh. Fujimura-sensei is
about to come barreling in.

164
00:11:43,100 --> 00:11:45,440
All right! I made it!

165
00:11:46,440 --> 00:11:47,979
Good morning, class!

166
00:11:47,980 --> 00:11:50,070
I'll take attendance now.

167
00:11:55,780 --> 00:12:00,449
Emiya, if you don't eat your
lunch soon, you won't get to.

168
00:12:00,450 --> 00:12:02,710
It's okay. I'm almost done.

169
00:12:06,380 --> 00:12:11,210
The heaters are one thing, but you didn't
have to agree to fix personal items too.

170
00:12:11,510 --> 00:12:12,669
Don't worry about it.

171
00:12:12,670 --> 00:12:14,760
Like they say, in for a
penny, in for a pound.

172
00:12:15,640 --> 00:12:17,720
There's such a thing
as being too considerate.

173
00:12:18,220 --> 00:12:22,600
Being helpful is all well and good,
but you should really learn to say no.

174
00:12:23,480 --> 00:12:25,980
You take "turn no one
away" too far, Emiya.

175
00:12:26,850 --> 00:12:28,980
Do I seem like that
much of a pushover?

176
00:12:30,150 --> 00:12:34,319
You're leaving yourself open to being
taken advantage of by the unscrupulous.

177
00:12:34,320 --> 00:12:37,369
Surely you could turn people
down every once in a while.

178
00:12:37,370 --> 00:12:40,869
What're you talking about?
Helping others is a good deed.

179
00:12:40,870 --> 00:12:43,409
That's not something the heir to a
temple should be complaining about.

180
00:12:43,410 --> 00:12:47,329
I'm just saying that you
take it too far, Emiya.

181
00:12:47,330 --> 00:12:50,749
If you keep going like
this, you'll burn out.

182
00:12:50,750 --> 00:12:52,760
Duly noted.

183
00:12:53,460 --> 00:12:55,760
Okay, all done!

184
00:13:36,170 --> 00:13:39,679
If you don't summon
yours soon, you'll die,

185
00:13:39,680 --> 00:13:40,970
Onii-chan.

186
00:13:53,150 --> 00:13:56,239
Of all the times
to come home late!

187
00:13:56,240 --> 00:13:59,740
I said in homeroom that it hasn't
been safe in town lately, remember?

188
00:14:00,280 --> 00:14:02,990
Um... Something came up.

189
00:14:04,040 --> 00:14:06,369
Do you get that
from Kiritsugu-san?

190
00:14:06,370 --> 00:14:08,702
I worry about what'll
happen to you if you keep

191
00:14:08,714 --> 00:14:10,959
spending all your time
trying to help people.

192
00:14:10,960 --> 00:14:13,089
Excuse me, Fujimura-sensei?

193
00:14:13,090 --> 00:14:15,759
Has Senpai always been this way?

194
00:14:15,760 --> 00:14:18,089
Yeah, for as long
as I've known him.

195
00:14:18,090 --> 00:14:22,969
Shirou just doesn't have it in
him to ignore people in need.

196
00:14:22,970 --> 00:14:25,849
"Comfort the afflicted, and
afflict the comfortable", you know?

197
00:14:25,850 --> 00:14:28,896
When he was a kid, he
wrote in an essay, "When

198
00:14:28,908 --> 00:14:31,900
I grow up, I wanna be
a champion of justice!"

199
00:14:32,270 --> 00:14:35,150
Wow, he must have been adorable.

200
00:14:35,530 --> 00:14:38,189
And whose fault
do you think that is?

201
00:14:38,190 --> 00:14:42,779
When kids grow up around immature adults,
they get funny ideas in their heads.

202
00:14:42,780 --> 00:14:45,909
If you don't like it, cook
your own damn food for once.

203
00:14:45,910 --> 00:14:47,080
What?

204
00:14:49,000 --> 00:14:51,370
You're going to make me cry!

205
00:14:52,460 --> 00:14:54,500
Sakura-chan, fill 'er up!

206
00:15:26,660 --> 00:15:28,410
Trace on.

207
00:15:32,370 --> 00:15:34,540
Tracing fundamental structure.

208
00:15:36,460 --> 00:15:38,420
Tracing auxiliary components.

209
00:15:39,090 --> 00:15:40,970
Altering fundamental structure.

210
00:15:47,470 --> 00:15:50,020
Reinforcing
auxiliary components.

211
00:16:08,950 --> 00:16:11,200
Damn, failed again.

212
00:16:12,790 --> 00:16:16,209
I can't believe that I still
can't do something this basic.

213
00:16:16,210 --> 00:16:18,630
I'm gonna be a novice forever.

214
00:16:21,960 --> 00:16:24,089
I just don't get it.

215
00:16:24,090 --> 00:16:27,890
How do I become a
champion of justice?

216
00:16:47,160 --> 00:16:49,280
Sakura, wait a second.

217
00:16:50,830 --> 00:16:52,160
Yes?

218
00:16:52,450 --> 00:16:53,960
What happened to your wrist?

219
00:16:55,790 --> 00:16:57,039
Shinji again?

220
00:16:57,040 --> 00:17:00,290
What's he thinking, raising
his hand against his little sister?

221
00:17:00,960 --> 00:17:03,709
N-No, that's not it, Senpai!

222
00:17:03,710 --> 00:17:08,050
I, um, got this when
I tripped and fell.

223
00:17:08,640 --> 00:17:10,850
You can't get a bruise
like that from tripping.

224
00:17:13,980 --> 00:17:14,980
I knew it.

225
00:17:15,100 --> 00:17:17,649
My brother had nothing
to do with this, I swear!

226
00:17:17,650 --> 00:17:20,230
I got hurt by
myself. That's all.

227
00:17:24,820 --> 00:17:28,530
Well, if you say so.
I'll leave it at that.

228
00:17:30,160 --> 00:17:32,949
Thank you. And
I'm sorry, Senpai.

229
00:17:32,950 --> 00:17:37,919
Why are you apologizing?
It's Shinji who's to blame.

230
00:17:37,920 --> 00:17:41,250
Do I smell your famous
rolled omelets, Shirou?

231
00:18:01,900 --> 00:18:03,359
What's up, Emiya?

232
00:18:03,360 --> 00:18:04,729
Let's eat.

233
00:18:04,730 --> 00:18:08,280
Sorry, Issei. I'm going to
eat in the cafeteria today.

234
00:18:08,610 --> 00:18:11,279
That's unusual. Did
something happen?

235
00:18:11,280 --> 00:18:12,330
Not really.

236
00:18:13,620 --> 00:18:14,620
Excuse me.

237
00:18:14,790 --> 00:18:16,040
Is Ryuudou here?

238
00:18:16,750 --> 00:18:18,119
I am, sir.

239
00:18:18,120 --> 00:18:19,790
What is it, Kuzuki-sensei?

240
00:18:22,170 --> 00:18:23,295
Change

241
00:18:23,296 --> 00:18:24,420
A Set

242
00:18:22,170 --> 00:18:23,295
B Set

243
00:18:23,296 --> 00:18:24,420
Lunch Lady Set

244
00:18:22,170 --> 00:18:23,295
Chef's Special

245
00:18:23,296 --> 00:18:24,420
Winter Special Oden Set

246
00:18:22,170 --> 00:18:23,295
Miso Ramen

247
00:18:23,296 --> 00:18:24,420
Soy Sauce Ramen

248
00:18:22,170 --> 00:18:23,295
Sliced Pork Ramen

249
00:18:23,296 --> 00:18:24,420
Rice Set

250
00:18:22,170 --> 00:18:23,295
Extra Noodles

251
00:18:23,296 --> 00:18:24,420
Fried Rice

252
00:18:22,170 --> 00:18:23,295
Curry Rice

253
00:18:23,296 --> 00:18:24,420
Pork Cutlet Curry

254
00:18:22,170 --> 00:18:23,295
Beef Bowl

255
00:18:23,296 --> 00:18:24,420
Pork Cutlet Bowl

256
00:18:22,170 --> 00:18:23,295
Extra Rice

257
00:18:23,296 --> 00:18:24,420
Miso Soup Set

258
00:18:27,720 --> 00:18:30,300
Going with the chef's special
for lunch today, are we?

259
00:18:30,590 --> 00:18:33,139
Not eating with the prez today?

260
00:18:33,140 --> 00:18:34,640
Nah.

261
00:18:36,220 --> 00:18:37,680
Say, Mitsuzuri...

262
00:18:38,390 --> 00:18:41,019
Has Sakura seemed
okay to you lately?

263
00:18:41,020 --> 00:18:42,149
Sakura?

264
00:18:42,150 --> 00:18:44,319
Yeah, she's
practicing her heart out.

265
00:18:44,320 --> 00:18:45,520
Oh.

266
00:18:45,820 --> 00:18:48,149
It's her brother
that's the problem.

267
00:18:48,150 --> 00:18:51,199
He's been taking his frustrations
out on the first-year boys.

268
00:18:51,200 --> 00:18:52,279
What frustrations?

269
00:18:52,280 --> 00:18:55,790
From what I hear, he got shot
down pretty hard by Tohsaka.

270
00:18:56,410 --> 00:18:57,450
By Tohsaka?

271
00:18:58,040 --> 00:18:59,620
Keep your voice down!

272
00:19:00,790 --> 00:19:04,790
Anyway, Shinji's been in a
foul mood ever since yesterday.

273
00:19:05,590 --> 00:19:10,300
I've had to keep an eye on him all
through practice, so I'm exhausted.

274
00:19:11,220 --> 00:19:13,889
Yeah, Shinji does
have a nasty temper.

275
00:19:13,890 --> 00:19:17,180
I feel like he might be planning to
get even with Tohsaka somehow.

276
00:19:18,020 --> 00:19:22,270
Nah, not even Shinji would go anywhere
near someone who'd rejected him.

277
00:19:23,770 --> 00:19:27,780
But he can't avoid her
if she comes to him.

278
00:19:28,980 --> 00:19:33,280
I'm not sure why, but Tohsaka's been
coming to watch at the dojo a lot lately.

279
00:19:34,120 --> 00:19:37,200
I guess you didn't know,
since you quit and all.

280
00:19:39,370 --> 00:19:42,079
But man, the look on
his face was hilarious!

281
00:19:42,080 --> 00:19:44,960
He practically pissed his pants!

282
00:19:52,590 --> 00:19:56,179
When Shinji gets
mad, he stays that way.

283
00:19:56,180 --> 00:19:57,430
Hey, you there!

284
00:20:01,980 --> 00:20:04,770
I hate to break it
to you, Matou Shinji,

285
00:20:05,150 --> 00:20:10,360
but Tohsaka Rin isn't gonna turn
up, no matter how long you wait!

286
00:20:14,410 --> 00:20:18,829
Maki, this guy doesn't match the
description Lady Mitsuzuri gave.

287
00:20:18,830 --> 00:20:20,789
He doesn't have
wavy hair, for one.

288
00:20:20,790 --> 00:20:24,579
Oh yeah? I bet he just
slicked it back with a little water!

289
00:20:24,580 --> 00:20:28,169
A face this stupid-looking
could only belong to Matou Shinji!

290
00:20:28,170 --> 00:20:30,379
You've got the wrong guy.

291
00:20:30,380 --> 00:20:33,669
See what I mean? That's
what the culprit always says.

292
00:20:33,670 --> 00:20:34,670
Wait.

293
00:20:36,550 --> 00:20:40,509
Sorry, but would you mind
showing us your student ID?

294
00:20:40,510 --> 00:20:42,020
S-Sure.

295
00:20:43,270 --> 00:20:44,656
Name - Shirou Emiya - Class - 2-C - Issued 4/1 -
The aforementioned is a student of this institution.

296
00:20:44,668 --> 00:20:44,940
Homurahara Academy

297
00:20:47,310 --> 00:20:49,819
See? It's not him, Maki-chan.

298
00:20:49,820 --> 00:20:52,069
Emiya? That Emiya?

299
00:20:52,070 --> 00:20:55,279
The guy who fixes our gear
whenever he has a spare moment?

300
00:20:55,280 --> 00:20:58,279
The one they call
"Homurahara's Brownie"?

301
00:20:58,280 --> 00:21:02,910
I've never heard that nickname before,
but I do know the track and field captain.

302
00:21:05,460 --> 00:21:10,879
Sorry. It seemed like you were looking
for someone, so we just assumed.

303
00:21:10,880 --> 00:21:14,799
That's okay. What was that
about Tohsaka not coming?

304
00:21:14,800 --> 00:21:16,050
Did something happen?

305
00:21:16,470 --> 00:21:19,549
She stayed home today.

306
00:21:19,550 --> 00:21:24,639
Yeah. Tohsaka's taking the
day off with a cold, good sir.

307
00:21:24,640 --> 00:21:26,761
It's hard to believe that
a flawless model student

308
00:21:26,773 --> 00:21:28,650
like her could even
get sick, though, right?

309
00:21:29,730 --> 00:21:34,189
We're sorry for the trouble our circus
attraction here caused you, Emiya.

310
00:21:34,190 --> 00:21:36,199
But you shouldn't
be here, either.

311
00:21:36,200 --> 00:21:39,739
Weren't you told that students with no
club activities should go straight home?

312
00:21:39,740 --> 00:21:41,160
Did something happen?

313
00:21:41,910 --> 00:21:43,409
You didn't know?

314
00:21:43,410 --> 00:21:46,910
There was a homicide by
the intersection near school.

315
00:21:48,080 --> 00:21:51,589
A family of four was attacked,
and only the youngest child survived.

316
00:21:51,590 --> 00:21:53,670
The parents and older
sister were stabbed to death.

317
00:21:54,840 --> 00:21:57,089
The killer is still at large,

318
00:21:57,090 --> 00:22:00,930
and the nature of the killings
has sparked considerable unrest.

319
00:22:01,760 --> 00:22:04,139
In Shinto, they've
got those gas leaks,

320
00:22:04,140 --> 00:22:07,229
while over here, we've got
these gruesome murders.

321
00:22:07,230 --> 00:22:11,190
It's only natural they'd be
sending students home early.

322
00:22:14,190 --> 00:22:21,200
DO NOT CROSS

323
00:22:31,210 --> 00:22:32,710
I know...

324
00:22:34,670 --> 00:22:38,550
Helping others and being a champion
of justice aren't the same thing.

325
00:22:44,760 --> 00:22:46,220
Ah, I see.

326
00:22:46,680 --> 00:22:47,730
Thank you.

327
00:22:58,650 --> 00:22:59,949
Hello.

328
00:22:59,950 --> 00:23:02,069
You must be Shirou-kun.

329
00:23:02,070 --> 00:23:03,819
I'll get straight to the point.

330
00:23:03,820 --> 00:23:06,735
Would you rather
be sent off to an

331
00:23:06,747 --> 00:23:10,620
orphanage, or taken in
by a man you just met?

332
00:23:31,850 --> 00:23:33,269
I'm glad.

333
00:23:33,270 --> 00:23:35,020
Then let's get you
dressed right away.

334
00:23:35,650 --> 00:23:39,280
You should get acclimated to
your new home as soon as possible.

335
00:23:39,610 --> 00:23:42,400
Oh, I forgot to
mention something.

336
00:23:43,320 --> 00:23:46,780
It's important that
you know this, all right?

337
00:23:48,200 --> 00:23:49,539
Well...

338
00:23:49,540 --> 00:23:51,579
For starters,

339
00:23:51,580 --> 00:23:55,460
I'm a magician.

340
00:24:01,630 --> 00:24:04,640
I've still got some
time before work.

341
00:24:11,850 --> 00:24:13,139
You're alive...

342
00:24:13,140 --> 00:24:15,480
You're alive! You're alive!

343
00:24:18,610 --> 00:24:21,280
Thank you. Thank you!

344
00:24:23,570 --> 00:24:25,450
I'm so glad I found someone.

345
00:24:26,910 --> 00:24:29,160
By saving even one person,

346
00:24:31,000 --> 00:24:32,410
I've saved myself.

347
00:24:35,330 --> 00:24:41,670
All I remember of that day ten years ago is
that it was hot, that I couldn't breathe,

348
00:24:42,380 --> 00:24:47,260
and that many others tried to save
people, only to die in the process.

349
00:24:48,430 --> 00:24:50,389
I hate that.

350
00:24:50,390 --> 00:24:53,680
It makes me angry to see
people die after trying so hard.

351
00:24:54,390 --> 00:25:00,940
Is it greedy of me to wish for a
happy ending, full of smiles for all?

352
00:25:02,440 --> 00:25:04,070
It's not that simple.

353
00:25:04,570 --> 00:25:09,450
Because that would involve saving
everyone without exception, Shirou.

354
00:25:09,950 --> 00:25:14,080
Kiritsugu's answer never
really convinced my younger self.

355
00:25:14,710 --> 00:25:21,460
After all, I knew he was an all-powerful
magician who had saved my life.

356
00:25:22,460 --> 00:25:29,720
So I asked Kiritsugu if he could
have saved everyone back then.

357
00:25:33,430 --> 00:25:34,930
But he said...

358
00:25:35,600 --> 00:25:36,939
Shirou.

359
00:25:36,940 --> 00:25:41,359
Saving one person
means not saving another.

360
00:25:41,360 --> 00:25:48,610
You see, a person can only save those
who are on the side they've chosen to take.

361
00:25:49,450 --> 00:25:51,200
It should be obvious, right?

362
00:25:52,030 --> 00:25:54,870
I mean, that's the very
definition of a champion of justice.

363
00:25:56,290 --> 00:25:58,619
I understand that now.

364
00:25:58,620 --> 00:26:02,130
Yeah, it is obvious... But...

365
00:26:02,710 --> 00:26:04,130
But I still hate it.

366
00:26:04,550 --> 00:26:08,130
Salvation shouldn't apply to
a limited number of people.

367
00:26:09,010 --> 00:26:13,640
I can't bear the thought of more strangers
dying around me like they did that day.

368
00:26:32,950 --> 00:26:34,450
That was Tohsaka just now...

369
00:26:35,370 --> 00:26:36,500
wasn't it?

370
00:26:42,920 --> 00:26:45,339
You shoulda said so sooner!

371
00:26:45,340 --> 00:26:47,419
If it's ramen you want, you've
come to the right person!

372
00:26:47,420 --> 00:26:48,549
Really, now?

373
00:26:48,550 --> 00:26:51,339
I happen to be an
expert on ramen!

374
00:26:51,340 --> 00:26:52,550
Where's Sakura?

375
00:26:53,180 --> 00:26:56,060
She went home early tonight.

376
00:26:56,350 --> 00:26:59,429
Why'd you send
her home by herself?

377
00:26:59,430 --> 00:27:04,190
Weren't you saying it wasn't
safe to go out alone at night?

378
00:27:05,320 --> 00:27:08,070
It's fine, it's fine. I sent
one of my men with her.

379
00:27:08,690 --> 00:27:10,950
You should've gone yourself.

380
00:27:11,320 --> 00:27:12,780
You're our teacher, after all.

381
00:27:13,950 --> 00:27:17,330
If I did that, I wouldn't get
to eat dinner until after ten!

382
00:27:17,660 --> 00:27:21,669
It's your fault for staying out
so late at your job, anyway!

383
00:27:21,670 --> 00:27:24,589
I always have to sit here
starving whenever you have work.

384
00:27:24,590 --> 00:27:29,420
If you're so hungry, why can't you
just get dinner at your own house?

385
00:27:30,510 --> 00:27:33,220
But this is my house.

386
00:27:34,640 --> 00:27:35,800
Sheesh.

387
00:27:37,180 --> 00:27:38,640
What's this?

388
00:27:40,980 --> 00:27:44,609
Oh, someone gave that to me,
but I don't want it, so you can have it!

389
00:27:44,610 --> 00:27:46,149
Why, thank you.

390
00:27:46,150 --> 00:27:47,570
But I don't want it either!

391
00:27:52,360 --> 00:27:55,780
You're sadly mistaken if you think
you can hit me with skills like yours.

392
00:27:56,370 --> 00:27:59,750
If you don't like it, I suggest
you practice some more.

393
00:28:01,290 --> 00:28:04,749
But more importantly,
Shirou, I'm famished!

394
00:28:04,750 --> 00:28:08,459
I've been waiting for ages,
so hurry up and make dinner!

395
00:28:08,460 --> 00:28:09,880
Yeah, yeah.

396
00:28:15,050 --> 00:28:19,809
Senpai, I won't be able to help with
the cooking for a while starting tonight.

397
00:28:19,810 --> 00:28:21,179
Is that all right?

398
00:28:21,180 --> 00:28:24,269
Don't worry about it.
It's the weekend, after all.

399
00:28:24,270 --> 00:28:26,060
I'm sure you have
people to hang out with.

400
00:28:28,320 --> 00:28:30,149
No, it's not like that!

401
00:28:30,150 --> 00:28:34,070
It's really just a personal thing,
and I'll still be going to club practices,

402
00:28:34,320 --> 00:28:38,869
so if anything comes up, please come
to the dojo, and I'll see what I can do!

403
00:28:38,870 --> 00:28:42,330
I wouldn't go out and have fun
just because it's the weekend!

404
00:28:44,920 --> 00:28:50,250
So... I'd appreciate it if you
didn't get the wrong idea.

405
00:28:50,960 --> 00:28:52,299
Understood.

406
00:28:52,300 --> 00:28:54,299
If something comes
up, I'll stop by the dojo.

407
00:28:54,300 --> 00:28:57,010
Thanks. That would be great.

408
00:28:58,510 --> 00:29:00,600
Senpai! Your hand!

409
00:29:03,390 --> 00:29:04,849
Where'd this come from?

410
00:29:04,850 --> 00:29:07,809
Did I cut myself while I was
tinkering with some old junk?

411
00:29:07,810 --> 00:29:11,019
It doesn't hurt or anything,
so it should fade soon.

412
00:29:11,020 --> 00:29:13,030
I'm fine. Nothing
to worry about.

413
00:29:13,440 --> 00:29:17,030
Okay. If you say so.

414
00:29:34,420 --> 00:29:36,970
Maybe I'm just tired.

415
00:29:41,680 --> 00:29:46,639
With your efforts, it looks like we'll have
all the equipment fixed before exams begin.

416
00:29:46,640 --> 00:29:48,189
Thank you again for your help.

417
00:29:48,190 --> 00:29:49,940
No problem. See you later.

418
00:29:57,700 --> 00:30:00,240
You think that was amazing?

419
00:30:02,700 --> 00:30:03,950
Shinji.

420
00:30:04,790 --> 00:30:07,460
Still at school, Emiya?

421
00:30:09,790 --> 00:30:12,460
I need to talk to you.
Come with me for a minute.

422
00:30:12,920 --> 00:30:15,299
A minute? Sorry.

423
00:30:15,300 --> 00:30:17,470
As you can see, I don't
have a minute to spare.

424
00:30:18,050 --> 00:30:21,089
Whatever your little
problem is, it can wait.

425
00:30:21,090 --> 00:30:22,350
Isn't that right, girls?

426
00:30:23,680 --> 00:30:25,179
Hang on, Shinji.

427
00:30:25,180 --> 00:30:27,730
This is about the
bruise on Sakura's wrist.

428
00:30:28,730 --> 00:30:30,559
What's this about Sakura?

429
00:30:30,560 --> 00:30:33,399
Don't dodge the question.
You hurt her again, didn't you?

430
00:30:33,400 --> 00:30:36,189
I don't know what you're
talking about, and I don't care.

431
00:30:36,190 --> 00:30:37,400
She's your sister, you know.

432
00:30:38,990 --> 00:30:40,819
Look, Emiya.

433
00:30:40,820 --> 00:30:43,079
You're starting to
get on my nerves.

434
00:30:43,080 --> 00:30:45,488
Yeah, we're brother
and sister, so that's all the

435
00:30:45,500 --> 00:30:47,870
more reason to mind
your own business, isn't it?

436
00:30:48,410 --> 00:30:50,329
You really don't
know how she got it?

437
00:30:50,330 --> 00:30:51,330
Nope.

438
00:30:51,830 --> 00:30:56,669
Or did Sakura tell
you that I beat her?

439
00:30:56,670 --> 00:30:57,340
No.

440
00:30:57,341 --> 00:30:58,879
There you go, then.

441
00:30:58,880 --> 00:31:02,840
It's not nice to make
baseless accusations, Emiya.

442
00:31:04,760 --> 00:31:07,640
I suppose. I'm sorry
I suspected you.

443
00:31:09,520 --> 00:31:12,439
If you're sorry, prove
it by doing me a favor.

444
00:31:12,440 --> 00:31:16,689
See, the dojo's in kind
of a mess right now.

445
00:31:16,690 --> 00:31:18,828
If you've got time to play
the concerned citizen,

446
00:31:18,840 --> 00:31:20,990
maybe you could do
something about it, Emiya-kun?

447
00:31:21,950 --> 00:31:25,159
Didn't Fujimura-sensei tell
you to clean it up, Senpai?

448
00:31:25,160 --> 00:31:27,949
That's right. You'd better...

449
00:31:27,950 --> 00:31:29,369
It's fine.

450
00:31:29,370 --> 00:31:32,450
I mean, if I start cleaning now, the
shop will be closed by the time I finish.

451
00:31:34,920 --> 00:31:37,049
Take it from here, will you?

452
00:31:37,050 --> 00:31:39,169
Wait, Senpai!

453
00:31:39,170 --> 00:31:41,630
We'll leave it to you, then.

454
00:31:52,850 --> 00:31:56,360
Man, this place never changes.

455
00:32:27,510 --> 00:32:28,510
Done.

456
00:32:43,320 --> 00:32:45,280
Who are they?

457
00:32:56,920 --> 00:32:57,920
Who's there?

458
00:33:29,370 --> 00:33:30,410
Hey.

459
00:33:52,760 --> 00:33:55,099
Today just wasn't
your lucky day, boy.

460
00:33:55,100 --> 00:33:58,599
Now that you're a
witness, I can't let you live.

461
00:33:58,600 --> 00:34:01,479
Dead men tell no
tales, and all that.

462
00:34:01,480 --> 00:34:04,990
Curse with your dying breath that you
were born with no luck and no power.

463
00:34:11,030 --> 00:34:13,539
You've given me some dirty work.

464
00:34:13,540 --> 00:34:16,120
How can I call myself
a hero after this?

465
00:34:16,960 --> 00:34:19,120
I understand. I'm
not complaining.

466
00:34:20,000 --> 00:34:21,789
I got a good look
at the girl's Servant.

467
00:34:21,790 --> 00:34:23,670
I'll be a good boy and return.

468
00:34:24,960 --> 00:34:28,300
Jeez. My Master's a
real nasty piece of work.

469
00:34:39,730 --> 00:34:42,150
He's not going to make it.
Not with a skewered heart.

470
00:34:46,400 --> 00:34:48,489
Don't do this to me...

471
00:34:48,490 --> 00:34:50,240
Why did it have to be you?

472
00:34:52,990 --> 00:34:55,620
Why did you have to pick this
hour, on this day, to be here?

473
00:34:57,870 --> 00:35:00,370
No. There's still a way.

474
00:35:26,360 --> 00:35:27,980
What happened?

475
00:35:58,770 --> 00:36:01,640
The man in blue
and the man in red...

476
00:36:04,650 --> 00:36:06,230
Who were those two?

477
00:36:07,110 --> 00:36:09,570
They were far beyond
ordinary humans.

478
00:36:10,360 --> 00:36:12,490
So I really was almost killed.

479
00:36:13,150 --> 00:36:14,150
No.

480
00:36:14,700 --> 00:36:17,950
Not "almost". I was killed.

481
00:36:25,920 --> 00:36:28,170
But here I am, alive.

482
00:36:29,090 --> 00:36:32,300
I was saved by someone
who came along afterward.

483
00:36:33,340 --> 00:36:35,509
Who could it have been?

484
00:36:35,510 --> 00:36:37,470
I wish I could at
least thank them.

485
00:36:50,900 --> 00:36:53,289
And here I was trying
to be considerate. I

486
00:36:53,301 --> 00:36:56,160
figured it'd hurt less if
you never saw it coming.

487
00:36:58,070 --> 00:37:01,909
Can't believe I got stuck with killing
the same person twice in one day.

488
00:37:01,910 --> 00:37:05,540
I guess the world's a bloody
place, no matter what the era.

489
00:37:05,830 --> 00:37:07,540
Trace on.

490
00:37:16,470 --> 00:37:19,050
Make sure you go into
the light this time, boy.

491
00:37:21,310 --> 00:37:23,770
Reinforcing
auxiliary components.

492
00:37:33,610 --> 00:37:35,400
That's an odd style.

493
00:37:38,780 --> 00:37:40,829
It's faint, but I sense mana.

494
00:37:40,830 --> 00:37:44,330
So that's why you're still alive after
taking my spear through your heart.

495
00:37:46,620 --> 00:37:48,580
This might be fun after all.

496
00:38:08,190 --> 00:38:11,610
I gave you a chance, but
you went and wasted it.

497
00:38:17,280 --> 00:38:19,450
If you're a man,
show some dignity.

498
00:38:28,750 --> 00:38:30,119
Checkmate.

499
00:38:30,120 --> 00:38:32,790
That last move was
pretty surprising, boy.

500
00:38:34,920 --> 00:38:37,339
I don't get it, though.

501
00:38:37,340 --> 00:38:40,589
You think fast on your feet,
but you're hopeless at magic.

502
00:38:40,590 --> 00:38:42,220
You seem to have
potential, though.

503
00:38:43,010 --> 00:38:45,720
Maybe you were
meant to be the seventh.

504
00:38:46,100 --> 00:38:49,139
Well, even if you were,
this is the end for you.

505
00:38:49,140 --> 00:38:50,900
Screw you!

506
00:38:53,820 --> 00:38:55,650
My life was saved.

507
00:38:56,320 --> 00:38:59,700
My life was saved, so I'm
not going to give it up so easily!

508
00:39:01,160 --> 00:39:04,659
I need to live. I
have to fulfill my duty.

509
00:39:04,660 --> 00:39:07,080
And I can't do that if I'm dead!

510
00:39:07,910 --> 00:39:10,670
I'm not gonna die for no
reason in a place like this,

511
00:39:12,630 --> 00:39:14,130
killed by a guy like you

512
00:39:15,130 --> 00:39:17,090
who takes lives
like it's nothing!

513
00:39:24,180 --> 00:39:25,720
The seventh Servant?

514
00:39:35,980 --> 00:39:36,980
I ask of you.

515
00:39:41,110 --> 00:39:44,910
Are you my Master?

516
00:39:52,960 --> 00:39:55,080
"Master"?

517
00:39:57,840 --> 00:40:01,720
I, the Saber-class Servant, have
come in response to your summons.

518
00:40:02,380 --> 00:40:03,800
Master, your orders.

519
00:40:07,510 --> 00:40:10,060
Henceforth, you hold
my sword in your hands,

520
00:40:10,480 --> 00:40:12,730
and I hold your fate in mine.

521
00:40:13,390 --> 00:40:15,310
Our contract is thus formed.

522
00:40:18,320 --> 00:40:19,820
What do you mean, "contract"?

523
00:41:02,650 --> 00:41:04,399
You coward!

524
00:41:04,400 --> 00:41:06,570
Why do you conceal
your own weapon?

525
00:41:11,950 --> 00:41:14,080
What's the matter,
Lancer? No self-respecting

526
00:41:14,092 --> 00:41:15,710
spearman stays
rooted to the spot.

527
00:41:16,250 --> 00:41:18,959
If you will not come to
me, I shall come to you!

528
00:41:18,960 --> 00:41:21,129
Before that, let me
ask you one thing.

529
00:41:21,130 --> 00:41:24,219
Your Noble Phantasm:
is it a sword?

530
00:41:24,220 --> 00:41:25,879
Who can say?

531
00:41:25,880 --> 00:41:28,550
It may be a battle axe.
Or perhaps it is a spear.

532
00:41:30,010 --> 00:41:33,930
Or it might even
be a bow, Lancer.

533
00:41:35,690 --> 00:41:38,270
Very funny, swordswoman!

534
00:41:38,650 --> 00:41:40,309
That stance...

535
00:41:40,310 --> 00:41:43,069
One more question.

536
00:41:43,070 --> 00:41:45,149
Since this is our first meeting,

537
00:41:45,150 --> 00:41:47,319
would you be interested
in calling it a draw?

538
00:41:47,320 --> 00:41:48,779
I think not.

539
00:41:48,780 --> 00:41:51,580
You will fall here, Lancer!

540
00:41:52,080 --> 00:41:53,409
Is that so?

541
00:41:53,410 --> 00:41:56,790
A shame. I was only
ordered to observe.

542
00:42:07,550 --> 00:42:09,890
I'll have your heart!

543
00:42:11,970 --> 00:42:12,970
Gae...

544
00:42:15,180 --> 00:42:16,600
Bolg!

545
00:42:50,760 --> 00:42:55,260
So you escaped my
mightiest blow, Saber.

546
00:42:58,730 --> 00:42:59,890
A curse?

547
00:43:00,650 --> 00:43:03,770
No, an attack that
reverses cause and effect?

548
00:43:04,320 --> 00:43:05,819
Gae Bolg...

549
00:43:05,820 --> 00:43:08,400
You are Ireland's
Child of Light!

550
00:43:09,650 --> 00:43:11,319
I messed up.

551
00:43:11,320 --> 00:43:14,660
If I use that
move, it has to kill.

552
00:43:16,830 --> 00:43:19,659
My lord is a coward, you see.

553
00:43:19,660 --> 00:43:22,880
You dodged my spear,
so he's ordering me home.

554
00:43:23,460 --> 00:43:24,630
You would run?

555
00:43:25,670 --> 00:43:27,880
You're more than
welcome to follow me.

556
00:43:29,010 --> 00:43:32,640
But if you do, be
prepared to die!

557
00:43:35,470 --> 00:43:36,560
Wait, Lancer!

558
00:43:36,810 --> 00:43:38,770
I-Is she crazy?

559
00:43:40,890 --> 00:43:42,310
Hey, are you all right?

560
00:43:47,610 --> 00:43:50,150
What the hell are you?

561
00:43:51,030 --> 00:43:53,820
As you can see, I am
a Saber-class Servant.

562
00:43:54,660 --> 00:43:56,870
As such, please call me "Saber".

563
00:43:59,290 --> 00:44:01,249
I'm Shirou.

564
00:44:01,250 --> 00:44:02,580
Emiya Shirou.

565
00:44:03,670 --> 00:44:04,710
Emiya...

566
00:44:06,960 --> 00:44:08,299
This house...

567
00:44:08,300 --> 00:44:11,550
No, that's not right. That
isn't what I want to ask you.

568
00:44:13,590 --> 00:44:14,969
I understand.

569
00:44:14,970 --> 00:44:17,640
You're not a legitimate
Master, are you?

570
00:44:19,770 --> 00:44:23,059
Nonetheless, you are my Master.

571
00:44:23,060 --> 00:44:26,610
Hang on. Isn't it kinda weird to start
calling me "Master" out of the blue?

572
00:44:27,770 --> 00:44:29,570
I shall call you "Shirou", then.

573
00:44:32,200 --> 00:44:36,070
Yes. I much prefer
the way that sounds.

574
00:44:38,830 --> 00:44:40,620
Wh-What are these?

575
00:44:41,750 --> 00:44:44,289
They are called Command Spells.

576
00:44:44,290 --> 00:44:46,330
Do try to avoid
using them carelessly.

577
00:44:47,540 --> 00:44:50,209
Shirou, my wounds,
if you please.

578
00:44:50,210 --> 00:44:51,799
You're asking me?

579
00:44:51,800 --> 00:44:54,629
Sorry, but complicated
magic like that is beyond me.

580
00:44:54,630 --> 00:44:57,050
I shall face them in my
current condition, then.

581
00:44:58,300 --> 00:45:00,139
There are two enemies outside.

582
00:45:00,140 --> 00:45:03,139
One more battle should
not pose a problem.

583
00:45:03,140 --> 00:45:04,980
Enemies outside?

584
00:45:06,310 --> 00:45:07,480
What do you mean?

585
00:45:15,610 --> 00:45:17,160
Stop, Saber!

586
00:45:23,660 --> 00:45:25,120
Are you mad, Shirou?

587
00:45:25,830 --> 00:45:29,499
I could have defeated them
handily, and you ordered me to stop!

588
00:45:29,500 --> 00:45:31,130
Just hold on, Saber!

589
00:45:31,460 --> 00:45:33,669
I have no idea what's going on.

590
00:45:33,670 --> 00:45:36,799
If I'm your Master,
at least fill me in!

591
00:45:36,800 --> 00:45:39,000
You would demand such a
thing with the enemy before us?

592
00:45:40,010 --> 00:45:45,230
Ah, so that's how it is,
my good novice Master?

593
00:45:50,190 --> 00:45:52,110
For starters, good evening,

594
00:45:53,570 --> 00:45:54,820
Emiya-kun.

595
00:46:10,300 --> 00:46:16,439
We didn't understand anything

596
00:46:16,440 --> 00:46:22,609
My left hand groped for
things that vanished to my touch

597
00:46:22,610 --> 00:46:25,609
A moral conflict

598
00:46:25,610 --> 00:46:28,410
stays your hand

599
00:46:28,660 --> 00:46:31,159
and tricks you

600
00:46:31,160 --> 00:46:33,040
out of your future

601
00:46:33,290 --> 00:46:39,959
I don't know how
to protect anyone,

602
00:46:39,960 --> 00:46:45,760
and my ideals might
well be pointless,

603
00:46:45,970 --> 00:46:53,970
but I want to live my life

604
00:46:54,970 --> 00:46:59,979
The past repeats before my eyes

605
00:46:59,980 --> 00:47:07,779
Here I will trust the me
that now stands with you

606
00:47:07,780 --> 00:47:13,869
Until my dream
crumbles and withers,

607
00:47:13,870 --> 00:47:19,499
I hope you will carve
out paradise with me

608
00:47:19,500 --> 00:47:23,210
Fight your fate

609
00:47:26,540 --> 00:47:28,659
I have no reason to fight.

610
00:47:28,660 --> 00:47:30,749
He's a certified
phony, that priest.

611
00:47:30,750 --> 00:47:32,419
Shirou is my Master.

612
00:47:32,420 --> 00:47:33,709
Berserker?

613
00:47:33,710 --> 00:47:36,919
Will you participate
in the Holy Grail War?

614
00:47:36,920 --> 00:47:39,840
Make your decision,
Emiya Shirou.

615
00:47:39,841 --> 00:47:40,930
The Curtain Rises

616
00:47:36,920 --> 00:47:40,930
Next Time

